@startuml
title EventBook — Level-1 Data-Flow Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false

actor Customer
actor Administrator
database "D1: Event and booking data\ndata.json" as D1
database "D2: Browser local storage\nfavourites + demo session" as D2

rectangle "1.0 Discover events\nand authenticate" as P1
rectangle "2.0 Create / manage\nbooking" as P2
rectangle "3.0 Create / edit\nevent and monitor bookings" as P3
rectangle "4.0 Validate role, input\nand remaining capacity" as P4

Customer --> P1 : search, login, event selection
P1 --> Customer : event list, details, role UI
P1 <--> D1 : read event metadata/capacity
P1 <--> D2 : local favourite and session data
Customer --> P2 : quantity and checkout confirmation
P2 --> Customer : confirmation, booking history, errors
P2 --> P4 : booking/cancellation request
P4 --> P2 : accepted/rejected result
P2 <--> D1 : booking and capacity updates
Administrator --> P3 : event data; booking action
P3 --> Administrator : metrics, status, validation feedback
P3 --> P4 : admin access and event validation
P4 --> P3 : accepted/rejected result
P3 <--> D1 : event/booking reads and writes

note bottom of P2
Payment-card fields do not flow to the API or data store.
end note
@enduml
